format 1
adapter curriculum 1
unit: radioactivity

lesson decay-chains
title: Decay chains
minutes: 4
xp: 50
teaches: u2-decay-chain
teaches: u2-decay-changes-not-vanishes
relies_on: u2-parent-daughter

description:
    One decay is not always the end. You will follow a nucleus that changes again and again, and see that every change makes a different nucleus and nothing simply vanishes.

cite ref-openstax-chem-21-3
supports: A daughter nuclide may be stable or may decay itself; uranium-238 reaches stable lead-206 in 14 steps.

cite ref-epa-radioactive-decay
supports: The uranium-238 and thorium-232 decay chains (optional card).

card c01
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l4-predict-daughter
scored: 0

card c02
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: Not always finished
figure: daughter-unstable
figure_at: 1

body:
    A nucleus decays into a daughter. The daughter can be unstable too. Then it decays again. The parent is the nucleus that decays. The daughter is the nucleus it becomes. Not every daughter is the end.

card c03
kind: sim
type: decay-chain
scored: 0
task: Tap the unstable nucleus to make it change. Keep going until it is stable.
hint: If the app says it isn't finished yet, tap again.

config:
    {
      "nodes": [
        {
          "id": "parent",
          "label": "Parent",
          "state": "unstable"
        },
