card c10
kind: teach
type: explain
scored: 0
title: A whole chain
figure: chain-zoom-out
figure_at: 1

body:
    Zoom out. One unstable nucleus can be the start of a whole chain of decays. Each step makes a new nucleus. The chain stops only when a stable nucleus is reached.

card c11
kind: item
type: item
item: u2-l4-choice-finished
connected: true

card c12
kind: teach
type: explain
tier: deeper
scored: 0
title: Go deeper: real chains
figure: real-chains
figure_at: 2

body:
    Real decay chains exist in nature. The uranium-238 chain ends in stable lead-206. The thorium-232 chain ends in stable lead-208. Some steps can branch in more than one way. There is nothing to memorise.
